  "facts": [
    "Ivica Tunnel, inaugurated in December 2010, stretches an impressive 2.2 kilometers, earning its place as Montenegro's second longest vehicular tunnel and a milestone in the country's modern infrastructure development.",
    "Carrying traffic between the mountain towns of Šavnik and Žabljak, Ivica Tunnel slices through the rugged Drobnjaci region, dramatically reducing travel time and connecting communities that once relied on winding, treacherous roads.",
    "Since its opening, Ivica Tunnel has become a vital artery for tourists and locals alike, facilitating smoother access to Žabljak's alpine resorts and boosting regional tourism."
